---
title: Platform Settings Reference
description: Complete reference for pika-config.ts platform configuration
---

Complete reference for the `pika-config.ts` file that controls global platform configuration.

## Overview

The `pika-config.ts` file is the central configuration for your entire Pika Platform instance. It defines:

- Project naming conventions across all stacks
- Site-wide feature defaults
- Global UI and behavior settings

{% aside type="caution" title="Protected File" %}
This file is protected from framework updates and will never be overwritten during sync operations.
{% /aside %}

## File Location

```
your-pika-project/
└── pika-config.ts
```

## Type Definition

```typescript
import type { PikaConfig } from 'pika-shared/types/chatbot/chatbot-types';

export const pikaConfig: PikaConfig = {
    // Configuration here
};
```

## Structure

The configuration is divided into two main sections:

1. **Project Names** - Naming conventions for infrastructure stacks
2. **Site Features** - Global feature configuration

## Project Names Configuration

Define naming conventions for all your infrastructure stacks. Each service gets its own name configuration.

### Name Formats

Each project requires five naming formats:

| Format | Description | Example | Usage |
|--------|-------------|---------|-------|
| `projNameL` | Lowercase, no separators | `mycompany` | Resource identifiers |
| `projNameKebabCase` | Lowercase with hyphens | `my-company` | URLs, file names |
| `projNameTitleCase` | PascalCase | `MyCompany` | Class names, CloudFormation resources |
| `projNameCamel` | camelCase | `myCompany` | JavaScript variables |
| `projNameHuman` | Human-readable | `My Company` | UI display |

### Required Project Configurations

#### pika (Core Service)

```typescript
pika: {
    projNameL: 'mycompany',
    projNameKebabCase: 'my-company',
    projNameTitleCase: 'MyCompany',
    projNameCamel: 'myCompany',
    projNameHuman: 'My Company'
}
```

The core Pika service that provides APIs, Lambda functions, and database infrastructure.

#### pikaChat (Chat Frontend)

```typescript
pikaChat: {
    projNameL: 'mycompanychat',
    projNameKebabCase: 'my-company-chat',
    projNameTitleCase: 'MyCompanyChat',
    projNameCamel: 'myCompanyChat',
    projNameHuman: 'My Company Chat'
}
```

The chat application frontend and infrastructure.

#### Additional Services (Optional)

You can add custom service names following the same pattern:

```typescript
weather: {
    projNameL: 'weather',
    projNameKebabCase: 'weather',
    projNameTitleCase: 'Weather',
    projNameCamel: 'weather',
    projNameHuman: 'Weather'
}
```

## Site Features Configuration

Global defaults for all features. Individual chat apps can override these settings.

### siteFeatures Object

```typescript
siteFeatures: {
    homePage: { /* ... */ },
    entity: { /* ... */ },
    userDataOverrides: { /* ... */ },
    // ... more features
}
```

### Home Page

Controls the platform home page appearance and navigation.

```typescript
homePage: {
    homePageTitle: string;
    welcomeMessage: string;
    linksToChatApps: {
        userChatAppRules: UserChatAppRule[];
    };
}
```

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `homePageTitle` | `string` | Page title displayed in browser |
| `welcomeMessage` | `string` | Welcome message shown to users |
| `userChatAppRules` | `UserChatAppRule[]` | Rules for which users see which chat apps |

**UserChatAppRule:**

```typescript
{
    userTypes: ['internal-user'], // User types who can see links
    chatAppUserTypes: ['internal-user', 'external-user'] // Types of apps to show
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
homePage: {
    homePageTitle: 'Acme Corp AI Assistants',
    welcomeMessage: 'Welcome! Choose an assistant below.',
    linksToChatApps: {
        userChatAppRules: [
            {
                userTypes: ['internal-user'],
                chatAppUserTypes: ['internal-user', 'external-user']
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

### Entity

Configure multi-tenancy with entities (accounts, organizations).

```typescript
entity: {
    enabled: boolean;
    attributeName: string;
    tableColumnHeaderTitle: string;
    displayNameSingular: string;
    displayNamePlural: string;
    searchPlaceholderText: string;
}
```

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `enabled` | `boolean` | Enable entity-based access control |
| `attributeName` | `string` | Custom data field name (e.g., `'accountId'`) |
| `tableColumnHeaderTitle` | `string` | Table column header text |
| `displayNameSingular` | `string` | Singular form (e.g., `'Account'`) |
| `displayNamePlural` | `string` | Plural form (e.g., `'Accounts'`) |
| `searchPlaceholderText` | `string` | Placeholder for search input |

**Example:**

```typescript
entity: {
    enabled: true,
    attributeName: 'organizationId',
    tableColumnHeaderTitle: 'Org ID',
    displayNameSingular: 'Organization',
    displayNamePlural: 'Organizations',
    searchPlaceholderText: 'Search organizations...'
}
```

### User Data Overrides

Allow certain users to override their custom data for testing.

```typescript
userDataOverrides: {
    enabled: boolean;
    promptUserIfAnyOfTheseCustomUserDataAttributesAreMissing: string[];
}
```

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `enabled` | `boolean` | Enable the user data override feature |
| `promptUserIfAnyOfTheseCustomUserDataAttributesAreMissing` | `string[]` | Prompt user if these fields are missing |

**Example:**

```typescript
userDataOverrides: {
    enabled: true,
    promptUserIfAnyOfTheseCustomUserDataAttributesAreMissing: [
        'accountId',
        'accountType',
        'region'
    ]
}
```

### Content Admin

Enable content administrators to view all user sessions for debugging.

```typescript
contentAdmin: {
    enabled: boolean;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
contentAdmin: {
    enabled: true
}
```

### Traces

Show AI execution traces for transparency.

```typescript
traces: {
    enabled: boolean;
    userTypes: UserType[];
    detailedTraces: {
        enabled: boolean;
        userTypes: UserType[];
    };
}
```

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `enabled` | `boolean` | Enable traces feature |
| `userTypes` | `UserType[]` | User types who can see traces |
| `detailedTraces.enabled` | `boolean` | Enable detailed technical traces |
| `detailedTraces.userTypes` | `UserType[]` | User types who see detailed traces |

**Example:**

```typescript
traces: {
    enabled: true,
    userTypes: ['internal-user', 'external-user'],
    detailedTraces: {
        enabled: true,
        userTypes: ['internal-user'] // Only internal users see details
    }
}
```

### Chat Disclaimer Notice

Display disclaimer messages in chat apps.

```typescript
chatDisclaimerNotice: {
    enabled: boolean;
    notice: string;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
chatDisclaimerNotice: {
    enabled: true,
    notice: 'This AI assistant provides general information. For critical decisions, consult a professional.'
}
```

### Verify Response

Enable AI self-correction and response verification.

```typescript
verifyResponse: {
    enabled: boolean;
    autoRepromptThreshold: 'A' | 'B' | 'C' | 'D';
    userTypes: UserType[];
}
```

| Threshold | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| `'A'` | Accurate and comprehensive |
| `'B'` | Accurate but incomplete |
| `'C'` | Accurate with unstated assumptions |
| `'D'` | Inaccurate |

**Example:**

```typescript
verifyResponse: {
    enabled: true,
    autoRepromptThreshold: 'C', // Auto-retry if C or worse
    userTypes: ['internal-user']
}
```

### Logout

Configure logout button visibility.

```typescript
logout: {
    enabled: boolean;
    userTypes: UserType[];
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
logout: {
    enabled: true,
    userTypes: ['internal-user', 'external-user']
}
```

### Site Admin

Configure the admin website features.

```typescript
siteAdmin: {
    websiteEnabled: boolean;
    supportUserEntityAccessControl: {
        enabled: boolean;
    };
    supportSpecificUserAccessControl: {
        enabled: boolean;
    };
    sessionInsights: {
        enabled: boolean;
    };
}
```

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `websiteEnabled` | Enable the admin site |
| `supportUserEntityAccessControl.enabled` | Enable entity-based access control in admin |
| `supportSpecificUserAccessControl.enabled` | Enable user-specific access control in admin |
| `sessionInsights.enabled` | Enable session insights in admin |

**Example:**

```typescript
siteAdmin: {
    websiteEnabled: true,
    supportUserEntityAccessControl: {
        enabled: true
    },
    supportSpecificUserAccessControl: {
        enabled: true
    },
    sessionInsights: {
        enabled: true
    }
}
```

### File Upload

Configure file upload capabilities.

```typescript
fileUpload: {
    enabled: boolean;
    mimeTypesAllowed: string[];
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
fileUpload: {
    enabled: true,
    mimeTypesAllowed: [
        'text/*',
        'application/pdf',
        'image/jpeg',
        'image/png',
        'text/csv'
    ]
}
```

### Suggestions

Quick suggestion buttons in chat interface.

```typescript
suggestions: {
    enabled: boolean;
    suggestions: string[];
    maxToShow: number;
    randomize: boolean;
    randomizeAfter: number;
}
```

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `enabled` | Enable suggestions feature |
| `suggestions` | Array of suggestion texts (usually overridden by chat apps) |
| `maxToShow` | Maximum suggestions to display |
| `randomize` | Whether to randomize order |
| `randomizeAfter` | Randomize after this many messages |

**Example:**

```typescript
suggestions: {
    enabled: true,
    suggestions: [], // Set per chat app
    maxToShow: 3,
    randomize: true,
    randomizeAfter: 0
}
```

### Prompt Input Field Label

Customize the chat input field placeholder.

```typescript
promptInputFieldLabel: {
    enabled: boolean;
    promptInputFieldLabel: string;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
promptInputFieldLabel: {
    enabled: true,
    promptInputFieldLabel: 'Ask me anything...'
}
```

### UI Customization

Global UI behavior settings.

```typescript
uiCustomization: {
    enabled: boolean;
    showUserRegionInLeftNav: boolean;
    showChatHistoryInStandaloneMode: boolean;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
uiCustomization: {
    enabled: true,
    showUserRegionInLeftNav: true,
    showChatHistoryInStandaloneMode: true
}
```

### Session Insights

Enable AI-generated session insights and analytics.

```typescript
sessionInsights: {
    enabled: boolean;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
sessionInsights: {
    enabled: true
}
```

### Tags

Enable custom UI tags and widgets.

```typescript
tags: {
    enabled: boolean;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
tags: {
    enabled: true
}
```

{% aside type="note" title="Tag Visibility" %}
Tag visibility is controlled at the tag definition level via `usageMode` and `status` fields, not in this configuration.
{% /aside %}

### Agent Instruction Assistance

Help users craft better prompts.

```typescript
agentInstructionAssistance: {
    enabled: boolean;
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
agentInstructionAssistance: {
    enabled: true
}
```

### Instruction Augmentation

Automatically enhance user prompts with additional context.

```typescript
instructionAugmentation: {
    enabled: boolean;
    type: 'llm-semantic-directive-search';
}
```

**Example:**

```typescript
instructionAugmentation: {
    enabled: true,
    type: 'llm-semantic-directive-search'
}
```

### User Memory

Remember user preferences and context across sessions.

```typescript
userMemory: {
    enabled: boolean;
    maxMemoryRecordsPerPrompt: number;
    maxKMatchesPerStrategy: number;
}
```

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `enabled` | Enable user memory feature |
| `maxMemoryRecordsPerPrompt` | Maximum memory records to include per prompt |
| `maxKMatchesPerStrategy` | Maximum matches per memory retrieval strategy |

**Example:**

```typescript
userMemory: {
    enabled: true,
    maxMemoryRecordsPerPrompt: 25,
    maxKMatchesPerStrategy: 5
}
```

## Complete Example

```typescript
import type { PikaConfig } from 'pika-shared/types/chatbot/chatbot-types';

export const pikaConfig: PikaConfig = {
    pika: {
        projNameL: 'acmecorp',
        projNameKebabCase: 'acme-corp',
        projNameTitleCase: 'AcmeCorp',
        projNameCamel: 'acmeCorp',
        projNameHuman: 'Acme Corp'
    },
    pikaChat: {
        projNameL: 'acmecorpchat',
        projNameKebabCase: 'acme-corp-chat',
        projNameTitleCase: 'AcmeCorpChat',
        projNameCamel: 'acmeCorpChat',
        projNameHuman: 'Acme Corp Chat'
    },
    siteFeatures: {
        homePage: {
            homePageTitle: 'Acme Corp AI Assistants',
            welcomeMessage: 'Welcome to Acme Corp AI Assistants!',
            linksToChatApps: {
                userChatAppRules: [
                    {
                        userTypes: ['internal-user'],
                        chatAppUserTypes: ['internal-user', 'external-user']
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        entity: {
            enabled: true,
            attributeName: 'accountId',
            tableColumnHeaderTitle: 'Account ID',
            displayNameSingular: 'Account',
            displayNamePlural: 'Accounts',
            searchPlaceholderText: 'Search for an account...'
        },
        userDataOverrides: {
            enabled: true,
            promptUserIfAnyOfTheseCustomUserDataAttributesAreMissing: ['accountId', 'accountType']
        },
        contentAdmin: {
            enabled: true
        },
        traces: {
            enabled: true,
            userTypes: ['internal-user'],
            detailedTraces: {
                enabled: true,
                userTypes: ['internal-user']
            }
        },
        verifyResponse: {
            enabled: true,
            autoRepromptThreshold: 'C',
            userTypes: ['internal-user']
        },
        fileUpload: {
            enabled: true,
            mimeTypesAllowed: ['text/*', 'application/pdf']
        },
        userMemory: {
            enabled: true,
            maxMemoryRecordsPerPrompt: 25,
            maxKMatchesPerStrategy: 5
        },
        sessionInsights: {
            enabled: true
        },
        tags: {
            enabled: true
        },
        strandsConverse: {
            enabled: false  // opt into Python Strands converse Lambda — see guides/advanced/strands-converse
        }
    }
};
```

## Best Practices

{% aside type="tip" title="Configuration Tips" %}
1. **Unique project names** - Avoid conflicts with AWS resource naming
2. **Start restrictive** - Enable features for internal users first, expand later
3. **Test changes locally** - Verify configuration before deploying
4. **Document customizations** - Add comments explaining non-obvious choices
5. **Version control** - Commit pika-config.ts changes with descriptive messages
{% /aside %}

## Validation

The configuration is validated at build time. Common errors:

- Missing required name formats
- Invalid user types (must be `'internal-user'` or `'external-user'`)
- Invalid threshold values
- Type mismatches

